-- The SIMPLYGO entry is the open reading, not an exclusion.
#ASSERT NOT (`the SC page excludes` (`purchase described as` `the base purchase` `SimplyGo as a descriptor`))
#ASSERT `only the SIMPLYGO entry would exclude` (`purchase described as` `the base purchase` `SimplyGo as a descriptor`)
#ASSERT NOT (`only the SIMPLYGO entry would exclude` `the base purchase`)

-- Fork F-sc-recurring: a standing-instruction charge that nothing else excludes is the case it touches.
#ASSERT `only the recurring-payment sentence would exclude` (`purchase paid by` `the base purchase` `Recurring payment arrangement`)
#ASSERT NOT (`only the recurring-payment sentence would exclude` `the base purchase`)
-- ... a standing-instruction charge that is also a cash advance, a premium or at a listed code is excluded either way.
#ASSERT NOT (`only the recurring-payment sentence would exclude` (`purchase paid by` (`purchase of kind` `the base purchase` `Cash advance`) `Recurring payment arrangement`))
#ASSERT NOT (`only the recurring-payment sentence would exclude` (`purchase paid by` (`purchase of item` `the base purchase` `An insurance premium`) `Recurring payment arrangement`))
#ASSERT NOT (`only the recurring-payment sentence would exclude` (`purchase paid by` (`recoded purchase` `the base purchase` 4900) `Recurring payment arrangement`))
